                <pb facs="0844" n="754" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg754"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-02T15:00:00+09:00">November 2, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 2—4:23 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>242. Department’s 149, August 29, 5 p.m. The spokesman of the Foreign Office
                    informed a member of my staff last evening that the Foreign Office reply to our
                    second representations in regard to the oil monopoly in Manchuria is practically
                    finished and will be delivered in a day or two. I therefore suggest awaiting
                    this communication before the Department decides on further action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
